
<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Find the horizontal and vertical intercepts or state that they don't exist for each function given below.
</p>
<ol>
<li><m>y=3x-1.5</m></li>
<li><m>f(x)=1-x^2</m></li>
<li><m>g(t)=5.4-0.2t</m></li>
<li><m>y=2x^3+16</m></li>
<li><m>h(m)=2\sqrt{m}-3</m></li>
<li><m> y=\dfrac{1}{x}</m></li>
<li><m>\displaystyle y=\frac{1}{x-1}</m></li>
</ol>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> 0.5; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> <m>-1.5</m>
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> <m>-1</m>, 1; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 1
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> 27; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 5.4
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> <m>-2</m>; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 16
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> 9/4; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> <m>-3</m>
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> none; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> none
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> none; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> <m>-1</m>
        </li>
    </ol>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>






<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Identify the horizontal and vertical intercepts for each function given numerically below.
</p>
<ol>
<li>\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline $x$ &$-2$ & $-1$ & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3
\\\hline $y$ & 3 & 0  & 2 & 2.5  & 0 & 4 
\\\hline
\end{tabular}

\vspace{5pt}</li>
<li>\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline $t$ &0 & 2 & 4 & 6 & 8 & 10
\\\hline $f(t)$ & 5 & 6  & 8 & 4  & 8 & 4 
\\\hline
\end{tabular}

\vspace{5pt}

\item\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline $x$ &3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8
\\\hline $g(x)$ & $-5$ & $-4$  & $-5$ & $-2$  & $-2$ & 0 
\\\hline
\end{tabular}</li>
</ol>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> <m>-1</m>, 2; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 2
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> none; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 5
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> 8; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> none
        </li>
    </ol>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>





<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Estimate the horizontal and vertical intercepts for each function given graphically below.
</p>
<ol>
<li>\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\begin{axis}[grid=both,
xmin=0,xmax=8.5,
ymin=-4.5,ymax=4.5,
xtick={0,1,...,8},
ytick={-4,...,4},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(t\), ylabel=\(y\),
x post scale = 1.2,
y post scale = 1.2
]
\addplot[domain=0:8] {4*sin(2*pi/8*deg(x))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}</li>
<li>\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\begin{axis}[grid=both,
xmin=-1.5,xmax=2.5,
ymin=-0.5,ymax=8.5,
xtick={-2,-1,...,3},
ytick={-8,...,8},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(y\),
x post scale = 1.2,
y post scale = 1.2
]
\addplot[domain=-2.5:2.5] {(x-1)^2+2};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}</li>
</ol>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> 0, 4, 8; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 0
        </li>
        <li>
            <alert>horizontal intercepts:</alert> none; <alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 3
        </li>
    </ol>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>







<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
A ball is dropped from a cliff above a lake. The ball's height above the surface of the lake, <m>h(t)</m>, in feet, <m>t</m> seconds after the ball is dropped, is given by
<me>
h(t)=300-16t^2.
</me>
Find the vertical intercept of the function <m>h(t)</m> and the horizontal intercept(s) for which <m>t\geq 0</m>. Give your answers to two decimal places and interpret the intercepts in practical terms.
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
<alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 300<mdash/>this is the number of feet above the lake that the ball is dropped from; <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> <m>t \approx 4.33</m><mdash/>this is the number of seconds that it takes after being dropped for the ball to hit the surface of the lake
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>







<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
The value of a car <m>V(t)</m>, in dollars, <m>t</m> years after the car was purchased is given by
<me>
V(t)=21500-1500t.
</me>
Find the vertical and horizontal intercepts of the function <m>V(t)</m> and interpret them in practical terms.
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
<alert>vertical intercept:</alert> 21500<mdash/>this is the price in dollars for which the car was purchased; <alert>horizontal intercept:</alert> <m>t \approx 14.33</m><mdash/>this is the number of years after purchase that it takes for the car's value to depreciate to <m>\$0</m>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>

